---
import "@styles/global.module.css";
import Cursor from "@components/cursor.astro";
import Footer from "@components/footer.astro";
import Header from "@components/header.astro";
import Meta from "@components/meta.astro";
import Scripts from "@components/scripts.astro";
---

<html>
    <head>
        <Meta name="Services" description="Check out my list of self-hosted services, including Forgejo and Akkoma! :3" />
        <Scripts />
        <Cursor />
        <style>
            .error {
                background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgb(136, 0, 0) 20%, rgb(78, 0, 0) 50%, rgb(150, 1, 1) 100%);
                color: white;
                border: 2px solid red;
                padding: 10px;
            }
        </style>
    </head>

    <body>
        <canvas id="background"></canvas>
        <!-- God damnit, I'm forced to use inline styles because Astro is stupid -->
        <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;">
            <Header />
            <main>
                <br />
                <div class="error">
                    <span>
                        <strong>Note:</strong>
                        <span>Running these services isn't free. If you have spare money, please <a href="/donate">donate</a>. Thank you!</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <h1>Self-hosted services</h1>
                <p>
                    I recently (2024/10/28) started self hosting a few pieces of software for my own use. Most of these services have registrations enabled, although registrations require approval. Here are some of my picks for what I host:
                </p>

                <h2>Akabot: Discord Bot</h2>
                <p>I maintain and run my own Discord bot. More on that is available <a href="https://akabot.xyz">in its project page</a>.</p>
                <p>There are 2 versions of Akabot that are run on my server. One is the public version and the other is a more private version.</p>

                <h2>Forgejo: Git server</h2>
                <p>I self-host an instance of Forgejo for my personal use. I host all of my code on it, mirroring it to other services and I also host mirrors of some of my favorite services.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://git.lunya.pet/Lunya">https://git.lunya.pet/Lunya</a> - This is my profile.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://git.lunya.pet/explore">https://git.lunya.pet/explore</a> - Here you can explore all of the public projects on this server.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Sharkey: The Fediverse</h2>
                <p>I run Sharkey for my Fedi software. Now on sk.lunya.pet since my old instance&apos;s DB was corrupted.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://sk.lunya.pet/@lunya">@lunya@sk.lunya.pet</a> - This is my profile.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://sk.lunya.pet">https://sk.lunya.pet/</a> - This is the main page of the software. It looks kinda cool with all the moving stuff, doesn't it? :3
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <p>Registrations are <strong>NOT</strong> open on my instance. Please go <a href="https://sharkey.fediverse.observer">find a different instance</a> to register at.</p>

                <h3>Akkoma: Additionally for backup and friends</h3>
                <p>There&apos;s an Akkoma instance for some of my friends on f.lunya.pet. The reason for this is that I migrated away from Sharkey after the database was broken.</p>
                <p>This instance might shut down after a while.</p>

                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://f.lunya.pet">https://f.lunya.pet</a> - Home page, public timeline only
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h3>GoToSocial: For bots</h3>
                <p>
                    I run a few bots on the fediverse, namely <a href="https://f.lunya.pet/users/collabmarkov">collabmarkov</a>, and a fast instance is something that&apos;s very useful for this. In thec configuration, the cooldown can be
                    disabled so I do not have to handle ratelimits.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://gts.lunya.pet">https://gts.lunya.pet</a> - GoToSocial home page. Currently there are no bots, they are yet to be migrated.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h2>PHPBB: Forums</h2>
                <p>I run my own forums. They feature a discussion for each of my projects, where anyone can create a topic and get help with anything.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="https://forums.lunya.pt">Home page</a> - The landing page. Feel free to explore, and feel free to make an account!</li>
                </ul>

                <h1>Fedi Services</h1>

                <p>Fedi services in this section refers to features like bots. This does not include Akkoma, which is listed above.</p>

                <h2>Collab Markov</h2>

                <p>Collab Markov is a silly bot that combines posts from many accounts and generates markovified posts based on them, on an hourly basis.</p>
                <p>More information about how this service works is on <a href="/project/collabmarkov">its page.</a></p>

                <ul>
                    <li><a href="https://fedi.lunya.pet/@collabmarkov">Collab Markov fedi account</a></li>
                </ul>
            </main>
            <Footer />
        </div>
        <script is:inline defer src="/scripts/background.js"></script>
    </body>
</html>
